{
  "info": {
    "_postman_id": "a6530113-b427-408a-bf17-b700f6e4e852",
    "name": "Activity6-CTADWEBL",
    "description": "Laboratory Activity 6 (File Management and Media Services) - tests image upload to Cloudinary for BulldogEx Shop products.\n\n1. Start the server first: npm run dev (inside marzan-server), and run npm run seed at least once so admin@bulldogex.nu.edu.ph and the starter products exist.\n2. Send the requests from top to bottom.\n3. UNLIKE every earlier activity's collection, 4 requests in folder 2 need a real image or non-image file attached by hand: open the request, go to Body, and click \"Select Files\" on the \"image\" field before pressing Send. Everything else runs with no manual step.\n   - 2.1 and 2.4: attach any real JPEG/PNG/WebP photo (under 5 MB).\n   - 2.2: attach any .txt or .pdf file (anything that is not an image).\n   - 2.3: attach any image file that is 5 MB or larger (e.g. a phone photo straight off the camera).\n4. Requests marked [Validation] are supposed to fail; their tests pass when the API rejects the request.\n\nFolder 3 deletes the temporary category and product this collection created, which also removes the uploaded image(s) from Cloudinary (asset cleanup) - check the Cloudinary Media Library before and after folder 3 to see the asset appear, then disappear.",
    "schema": "https://schema.getpostman.com/json/collection/v2.1.0/collection.json"
  },
